-- title:
--   Powers of t generate S modulo (p,φvarpi)
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative local ring whose maximal ideal is principal, generated by an element $\varpi$, and let $S$ be a commutative noetherian local ring. Suppose given a ring homomorphism $\varphi : A[X] \to S$ from the polynomial ring over $A$ such that the maximal ideal of $S$ is generated by the two elements $\varphi(\varpi)$ and $t := \varphi(X)$ (writing $\varphi(a)$ for the image of the constant polynomial $a$), and such that $\varphi(\varpi)$ is a prime element of $S$. Suppose further given a ring homomorphism $\chi_0 : S \to \kappa$ to the residue field of $A$ whose kernel is exactly the maximal ideal of $S$ and which is compatible with the residue map of $A$ on constants, i.e. $\chi_0(\varphi(a))$ is the residue class of $a$ for every $a \in A$. Then for every prime element $p$ of $S$ that is not associated to $\varphi(\varpi)$ there exists a natural number $n$ such that every $x \in S$ admits coefficients $c_0,\dots,c_{n-1} \in A$ with $x - \sum_{i<n} \varphi(c_i)\, t^{\,i}$ lying in the ideal of $S$ generated by $p$ and $\varphi(\varpi)$.
--
--   The conclusion says that the quotient $S/(p,\varphi\varpi)$ is generated as an $A$-module by the powers $1,t,\dots,t^{n-1}$, i.e. that $S/(p)$ is quasi-finite over $A$ at its closed point; this finiteness is the hypothesis needed to apply Zariski's main theorem. It is used in the proof of [`HenselianLocalRing.forall_exists_monic_dvd_eval_of_prime_of_not_associated`](thm.html#HenselianLocalRing.forall_exists_monic_dvd_eval_of_prime_of_not_associated), which produces a monic polynomial over $A$ annihilated by a prime element of such an $S$.
